{
  "_": [
    "States captured for each app before and after a styling change. A state is a URL, a",
    "theme, a viewport and optionally a few actions to reach a screen that is not the first.",
    "Kept as data rather than in the script so that what is covered is reviewable, and so",
    "adding a screen to the net is a one-line change.",
    "Selectors here must not name a CSS class. A styling migration deletes classes, and a state that selects by one silently starts photographing a different screen \u2014 which is exactly what happened to madlib's writer. Roles and text survive.",
    "An app that shows something random needs that value pinned, or its baseline can never be stable \u2014 hat draws a fresh number on every load, so its states carry the app's own share parameters to fix the result at 42."
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "viewports": [
      {
        "name": "desktop",
        "width": 1280,
        "height": 900
      },
      {
        "name": "mobile",
        "width": 390,
        "height": 844
      }
    ],
    "themes": [
      "light",
      "dark"
    ],
    "wait": 1200
  },
